  S~S The Idea of an Elevator Pitch

    The README file is the publisher's one chance to make the elevator pitch.

    Imagine you are at the big convention where your product is first introduced.  You wait at the
    elevator upstairs and find you are next to the boss of the company that might buy your product.

    The boss has never heard of you, or your company, or your product.

    The boss boards the elevator, you board.
    The boss picks the convention floor and smiles "same?"; you nod your head and smile back.

    The door shuts.  You have 30-45 seconds... Go!

  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   [edit: go for it]

  S~S The Elevator Pitch

    Signal algorithms cause electronic signal and sensor components to exchange information.

    The SimpleSal Signal Algorithm Laboratory is free source code software. It supports a novice
    developer's desire to imagine, write and then run signal algorithms in a safe and controlled
    application environment.  A step above setup() and loop(); a hint of an RTOS; debuggable.

    The parallel in computer history is the programming language BASIC.  It enables an introduction
    to writing software algorithms that perform a useful task using the resources of a computer.

    The rest is up to you.  Enjoy the convention.

  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   [edit: nice]

    Ding.  Elevator door opens.

