  S~S The value of a 3-legged footstool

    What is the increase in complexity when moving from three legs to four legs?  It is the
    addition of the fourth leg that creates a need in the design for parallel lines and symmetry.
    The four-legged footstool wobbles usually; the three-legged footstool is stable anywhere.
    It probably is never truly level across the surface, but it is stable to stand on.

    The SimpleSal three-legged stool is built from:

    1) the published software in the repo:
        GitHub username SimpleSal, simplesal repository, branch main-simplesal

    2) the information within the published software about how to make use of SimpleSal software:
        \SimpleSal\ssDocs\Find and Open Documents.html          <web browser viewable>

    3) the information about how to write signal algorithms using software
        simplesal's substack.com website, most content free without a subscription, see below

------------------------------------------

  S~S Published information outside the repo's human metadata AND repo metadata.

    This text is not-clickable information about the free SimpleSal ecosystem of code and documents.

    The site includes pretty documents with colorful drawings constructed from circles and arrows.

        Also, videos showing the effect of the annotated software being shown alongside the effect.

    simplesal.substack.com          user "simplesal" on site "substack.com"

